From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:11:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] rocket: rk3576: zero-copy CONCATENATION along the
 channels

In the NPU's NC1HWC2 layout a concatenation input that starts at a
channel offset that is a multiple of 16 is a byte range of the output.
Make each such input a view of the output BO (rkt_resource_view), so its
producer writes straight into the concatenation and nothing runs for the
concatenation itself. All inputs and the output need the same
quantization and spatial size, and every input but the last a multiple
of 16 channels.

Jobs and invokes that depend on a concatenation output depend on the
producers of its inputs; the two-core planner passes the row ranges of
the concatenation's consumers through to them.

As a tensor can only be a view of one output, rkt_ml_operations_filter()
claims a tensor as the input of at most one concatenation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6ragSxZN7WKWgGsfgrMX1
